-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  test_mode.pcpp - Unit testing compliance: @unitTestMode on

  With @unitTestMode on (BNF.md sec 8) an exe starts as always: the units'
  initialize sections, then its own; then the runner runs the tests of every
  unit it imports, then its own (the body does not run); finalize runs in
  reverse; the exit code is the number of failed tests (2 here: one fails an
  assert, one raises). @unitTestMode off: test_mode_off.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\test_mode.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\test_mode.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    unit init
    main init

    ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
    ║                     Unit Test Runner                         ║
    ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

    Running 4 test(s)...

    ✅ PASS: unit adds
    ✅ PASS: passes
    ❌ FAIL: fails
      🔴 <DIR>/test_mode.pcpp:93: testAssertEqualInt failed: expected 1, got 2
      🔴 <DIR>/test_mode.pcpp:94: testFail: why
    ❌ FAIL: raises
      🔴 <DIR>/test_mode.pcpp:97: test raised exception 7: inside

    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Results: 2 passed, 2 failed, 4 total
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    main final
    unit final
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 2
  <DIR> is the folder this file is in, as the compiler prints it
  (its full path, forward slashes).
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    test_mode_err_value.pcpp
      @unitTestMode takes on or off (SM0100)
    test_mode_err_lib.pcpp
      @unitTestMode in a lib: no program runs its tests (SM0110)
    test_mode_err_lib_tests.pcpp
      a test block in a lib never runs (SM0113, a warning: it still builds)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe test_mode;

@unitTestMode on;

import test_mode_unit;

initialize
begin
  println("main init");
end;

finalize
begin
  println("main final");
end;

begin
  println("the body does not run in test mode");
end.

test "passes"
begin
  testAssertEqualInt(4, test_mode_unit.Add(2, 2));
end;

test "fails"
begin
  testAssertEqualInt(1, test_mode_unit.Add(1, 1));
  testFail("why");
end;

test "raises"
begin
  raisecode(7, "inside");
end;
